          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS supports NIST 800-88, HIPAA, ISO/IEC 27001:2022, SOC 2, and DoD 5220.22-M for documented media handling on Bakersfield electronics recycling projects. Each Kern County engagement includes chain of custody records and a Certificate of Destruction for the compliance file. NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 requires methods that render target data recovery infeasible using state of the art laboratory techniques, the requirement STS destruction meets for Bakersfield organizations. Serial-level reporting helps Corporate IT Directors at Chevron and healthcare teams at Kern Medical document downstream handling without extra vendors."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS provides scheduled commercial pickup across Bakersfield and Kern County, including Rosedale, Oildale, Downtown Bakersfield, Southwest Bakersfield, and East Bakersfield. Routes also cover Delano, Wasco, Shafter, Taft, Tehachapi, and Highway 99 freight corridors. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me throughout Bakersfield find STS provides scheduled pickup in Rosedale, Oildale, and all Kern County locations. Complimentary pickup is available for qualifying volumes serving energy, healthcare, agriculture, and public agencies across the metro."
          }
        },
        {
