            "text": "Yes. Pickup is free for qualifying volumes on scheduled commercial routes serving Bakersfield and Kern County. Send an equipment list and STS confirms eligibility, timing, and dock access before a truck is dispatched. Qualifying Bakersfield offices, packing plants, clinics, and municipal sites typically receive complimentary collection with no hidden fees. Volume discounts and asset recovery credits may offset remaining processing costs after sanitization and material recovery are complete."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Serial-level reports, chain of custody logs, and Certificates of Destruction are included with every scheduled Bakersfield pickup for audit files. Corporate IT Directors typically expect detailed certificates of destruction for audit reviews, included in every STS service engagement. Accurate reporting helps Kern County teams support HIPAA, SOX, and CalRecycle reviews without hiring extra vendors. Certificates typically issue within 48 hours of completed processing for Chevron, Kern Medical, and similar regulated employers."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Bakersfield organizations typically receive same-week pickup after STS reviews a complete inventory list. Larger clinic, campus, or plant refreshes are scheduled around production and academic calendar windows. Kern High School District refreshes usually follow academic calendars, while plant pickups for growers such as Grimmway Farms follow harvest and shutdown windows. Dock access, media counts, and Highway 99 routing are confirmed before the truck is dispatched."
